PAGE RISKS (from the page specs, no file change)

- Teddy page tail: l2-w07-story-page-is-it-a-teddy-no holds both guards the task asks about. It references the Pip render (picture 6). It states: ONLY the fluffy golden-brown tip of a tail sticks out from under the blanket; no puppy body, no head, no ears, no legs, and no collar show. The count line ends: exactly two children, one blanket, one thought bubble with one teddy bear, and one tail tip. Advice: at page review check one tail tip and no other puppy part; re-run with the negative list kept first if a whole puppy returns.
- Thought-bubble toy pages: six pages use the six-toy sheet. Each colorPrompt lists all six toys, then says draw ONLY the named toy once, repeats draw only this ONE toy and no other toy anywhere in the bubble sentence, and ends with a count of exactly one toy in the bubble. The wording is clear and stated three times. Advice: at page review count one toy per bubble and no toy elsewhere; re-run extra-toy pages with the one-toy sentence kept first.

